# fixedbugs, defect 2036's finding, pinned 2026-10-13 as a known cost.
#
# SYMPTOM: a header of the program's own whose `printf((const char *)L"x")`
# reads a wide literal's bytes as its format is refused `ffi_header_refused`
# at exit 1, `format string should not be a wide string [-Werror,-Wformat]`.
#
# REASON: C defines the call: a pointer to an object converts to a pointer to
# a character type, through which its bytes are read (C11 6.3.2.3p7, 6.5p7),
# and the format is those bytes up to the first null; but clang files the
# diagnostic under `-Wformat` itself, under none of its parts, and the region
# keeps `-Wformat` an error for the conversion its argument does not match,
# which reads the wrong bytes (defect 2034); no pragma reaches one of its own
# diagnostics alone (`emit/header_region.hero`).
#
# RULING: the author's, 2026-10-13, a known cost: robustness first (design.md
# §1.12). Revisit if clang gives this diagnostic a flag of its own; this
# golden moves when the region can pass it over.

extern "fixedbugs-2036-a-header-s-printf-of-a-wide-literal-read-as-bytes-is-a-known-cost.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function fmt_shape() -> i32

function main()
    print(fmt_shape())
